From 37dbf8a8de53273587c01e0e3c5b492cd293e01b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@localhost>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:33:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] omatel 0.3.0: MMS and group messages through mmsd-tng

The agent becomes mmsd-tng's client (org.ofono.mms on the session bus).
It follows mmsd-tng as it comes and goes, imports what GetMessages lists
when it appears, then follows MessageAdded, MessageRemoved, the
messages' PropertyChanged("status") and MessageSendError.

A received MMS is stored like an SMS: committed first (its text from the
text/plain parts, every other part copied out of mmsd-tng's PDU file into
parts/<uuid>/ in the data directory), then deleted from mmsd-tng. The
store keys MMS by mmsd-tng's object path (a unique index), so a crash in
between or a message reported twice stores nothing twice. A group
conversation is the sender and the recipients minus the phone's own
numbers (mmsd-tng's Modem Number, ModemManager's OwnNumbers), with the
store's sorted, comma-joined address; each message keeps its sender.
Notifications say "Picture" or "Attachment" for a message with no text,
and name the sender in a group.

Sending: Messages1 gains SendWithAttachments(as, s, a(ss)) and
SendToConversationWithAttachments(x, s, a(ss)), ListParts(x) -> a(ssx)
and the MmsReady property; the 0.2 members are unchanged, except that a
group conversation's text now goes as MMS. The agent picks the
transport: text to one person stays SMS, anything with an attachment or
to a group is MMS. Attachments are copied into parts/out-<id>/ before the
call returns; the stored message follows mmsd-tng's sent,
sending_failed and delivered, and leaves mmsd-tng once nothing more can
happen to it (48 hours at most for a delivery report). The carrier's
size limit is checked first so "too big" is said plainly. Without
mmsd-tng the message is kept as failed with that reason, Retry sends it
later, and the new calls answer ...Messages1.Error.MmsUnavailable.

The apps delete messages straight in the store, so schema 2 adds triggers
that list deleted messages' mmsd-tng paths and part files; the agent
deletes those from mmsd-tng and from disk at attach and every ten minutes,
and a forgotten path is never imported again. An MMS that mmsd-tng still
holds is no longer failed at start-up as "interrupted".

Tests: store tests for MMS inserts, parts, groups and the forgotten
lists; a scripted mmsd-tng in omatel-mock (shapes from mmsd-tng 2.6.4's
service.c) and tests/mms.rs driving the agent against it on a private
session bus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
